  "text": "9:41¢ all ¥ @\npa eee xx\nhe talks about how getting under 6.5 hours literally\nmakes our brain acutely insulin resistant, triggering\nconstant decision fatigue and craving stimulants.\nit traps us in that vicious cycle: stress steals our\nsleep, and poor sleep sabotages our resilience.\nhe suggests approaching your rest like a curious\nscientist rather than someone who is broken. &\nstarting with tiny, gentle levers—like cutting harsh\nbathroom overhead lights an hour before bed, or\nexploring calming minerals like magnesium glycinate\n(200-500 mg) to relax tight muscles. +\nwhat feels like the loudest thing keeping you wired\nwhen your head finally hits the pillow right now? §\nhere's what you can ask next\nwhy is my mind so loud at night?\nhow do i quiet my racing thoughts?\nmeditation for deep restful sleep\nask eve al.. wv)\neve ai provides general information only. it is not\nmedical, financial, therapeutic, or professional advice,\nand may not reflect mindvalley’s views or always be\naccurate.\n",
